{
    "Replace_Clip_By_Min_Max":
    {
        "Introductions":
        [
            "============================================================================",
            "DESCRIPTION: Replace Clip with Min and Max operations",
            "============================================================================",
            "This transformation decomposes a Clip node with both minimum and",
            "maximum inputs into two elementary operations: Min followed by Max.",
            "The intermediate Min output is connected to the Max input, and the",
            "final Max output keeps the original Clip output name.",

            "MATCH CONDITION:",
            "- The node operator is Clip",
            "- The Clip data input is {node.input[0]}",
            "- The minimum input is {node.input[1]}",
            "- The maximum input is {node.input[2]}",

            "MATHEMATICAL EQUIVALENCE:",
            "Clip(x, min, max) = Max(Min(x, max), min)",
            "The bounds must satisfy min <= max for the usual clipping behavior.",

            "TRANSFORMATION STEPS:",
            "1. Find a Clip node with data, minimum, and maximum inputs",
            "2. Remove the original Clip node",
            "3. Create a Min node using the data input and maximum input",
            "4. Store the Min result in an intermediate tensor",
            "5. Create a Max node using the intermediate tensor and minimum input",
            "6. Reuse the original Clip output name for the final Max output",

            "EXAMPLE:",
            "Original graph: Clip(input, min_value, max_value)",
            "input = [-2.0, 0.5, 4.0], min_value = 0.0, max_value = 1.5",
            "Original output: Clip(input, 0.0, 1.5) = [0.0, 0.5, 1.5]",
            "Replacement graph:",
            "  1. Min(input, max_value) = Min([-2.0, 0.5, 4.0], 1.5)",
            "                    = [-2.0, 0.5, 1.5]",
            "  2. Max(min_result, min_value) = Max([-2.0, 0.5, 1.5], 0.0)",
            "                              = [0.0, 0.5, 1.5]",

            "RESULT: Equivalent computation using Min followed by Max",
            "============================================================================"
        ],
        "SearchBy":
        {
            "nodes": [
                {
                    "op_type": "Clip",
                    "inputs": [
                        
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        "ReplaceBy":
        {
            "graph": {
                "nodes": [
                    {
                        "name": "{node.name}",
                        "Action": "Remove"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Min_replace_for_{node.name}_{node.index}",
                        "op_type": "Min",
                        "inputs": [
                            "{node.input[0]}",
                            "{node.input[2]}"
                        ],
                        "outputs": [
                            "Min_replace_for_{node.name}_{node.index}_output"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Max_replace_for_{node.name}_{node.index}",
                        "op_type": "Max",
                        "inputs": [
                            "Min_replace_for_{node.name}_{node.index}_output",
                            "{node.input[1]}"
                        ],
                        "outputs": [
                            "{node.output[0]}"
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            }
        }
    }
}